      "username": "fjur",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-05-28T17:24:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"rjc917\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rjc917/48/1888_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> rjc917:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Now I’m wondering how it was determined exactly how big each of those stat bars should be.&nbsp; Obviously they can be generally figured out e.g.&nbsp;this spirit is really good at defense, but doesn’t produce much fear so fear should be low and defense should be high, but is there some formula for exactly how big to make them?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Well, if you look at the Template page on the Spirit Island Wikia it says that there are 5 levels for each.</p>",
